Let x be the oxidation number of Cr in $\mathrm{CrO}_4^{2-}\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore & x+4 \times(-2)=-2 \\
& x-8=-2 \\
\therefore & x=8-2=+6
\end{array} \\ Let $y$ be the oxidation number of Cr in $\mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore \quad & 2 \times(+1)+2(y)+7 \times(-2)=0 \\
& +2+2 y-14=0 \\
& 2 y=12 \\
\therefore \quad & y=+6
\end{array}

